WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.818
[MUSIC]

00:00:08.818 --> 00:00:13.834
&gt;&gt; In every industry, there is some
company that really makes a difference.

00:00:13.834 --> 00:00:19.568
And in ever one of those companies,
there's a leader who really mattered.

00:00:19.568 --> 00:00:25.072
Our vision at the Stanford Executive
Program is to help you become that leader.

00:00:25.072 --> 00:00:31.852
[MUSIC]

00:00:31.852 --> 00:00:36.956
Our curriculum will bring you to
the cutting edge in the latest

00:00:36.956 --> 00:00:42.370
thinking on business excellence,
design thinking, big data.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.413
The latest in financial engineering.

00:00:44.413 --> 00:00:46.270
Strategic management.

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:48.860
Methods for innovation.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:54.290
The faculty at the Stanford Business
School focus on why companies win.

00:00:55.490 --> 00:01:00.210
How public policy shapes the success and
failure of economies.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.891
How people and their careers change.

00:01:02.891 --> 00:01:08.290
How negotiations, improve or
hurt the chances of a business.

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:13.060
How groups and teams operate
effectively to get the job done.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:17.626
Helping you to understand what will make
a difference for you as a leader and for

00:01:17.626 --> 00:01:19.438
your company as a competitor.

00:01:19.438 --> 00:01:23.616
[MUSIC]

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:28.175
Our approach to learning in
the Stanford Executive Program

00:01:28.175 --> 00:01:32.003
relies on a great deal of collaboration,
as you,

00:01:32.003 --> 00:01:37.860
together with the executives in
the program, share your experiences.

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:42.040
You'll carry with you that network
that you create when you're here.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:45.714
So that over your career,
your relationships worldwide

00:01:45.714 --> 00:01:50.702
in the business community will be enriched
by the six weeks that you had here.

00:01:50.702 --> 00:01:53.696
[MUSIC]

00:01:53.696 --> 00:01:57.070
You will be changed by
your experience here.

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:00.530
In the short run,
you will have specific plans and

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:04.540
tools that you can execute on Monday
morning when you return to work.

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:10.590
And in the long run, your career and
your business will go onto

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:15.680
a different trajectory because of
the techniques and ideas that you learned.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.236
We're excited about the directions
your career will be taking.

00:02:21.236 --> 00:02:23.325
We look forward to seeing
you here at Stanford.

00:02:23.325 --> 00:02:32.450
[MUSIC]

